    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d885">

                <pb facs="1017" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–2945</note>
                <head>No. 885<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States Delegation Working
                        Paper</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d885-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-29">July 29, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for Mr. Clayton</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summary on German Economic and
                        Related Matters</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">General Understanding</hi>—There will have to be one or
                    more basic memoranda on <hi rendition="#italic">boundaries;</hi> “zonal”
                    handling of <hi rendition="#italic">reparations</hi>, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supply.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Economic Principles</hi>—There is already agreement on
                    principles 10–17.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d885-f2"/> Further action:<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d885-f3"/>
                    <list>
                        <label><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>.</label>
                        <item>Delete Principle No. 18.</item>
                        <label><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>.</label>
                        <item>In view of the decision in fact to give up quadrilateral action on
                            reparations operations and on programming, procuring and financing of
                            imports, the last sentence of paragraph 14 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >d</hi>), already tentatively agreed by the Foreign Ministers,
                            should be amended to read as follows: “except where determined by the
                            occupying power concerned to be required for the payment for necessary
                            imports, no grant or credit to Germany or Germans by any foreign persons
                            or governments shall be permitted”. If agreement cannot be reached with
                            the Russians on this amendment, we should insist on the deletion of the
                            entire sentence.</item>
                        <label><hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</label>
                        <item>A minor improvement would be effected in the document by the following
                            two amendments to paragraph 13: <quote rend="blockquote">
                                <list>
                                    <item>“(<hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                                            >Currency and banking</hi>, central taxation and
                                        customs;”</item>
                                    <item>“(<hi rendition="#italic">g</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                                            >Transportation and Communications”</hi></item>
                                </list></quote>
                        </item>
                    </list></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Reparations</hi>—Mr. Pauley’s memo of July 24.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d885-f4"/></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Restitution</hi>—Our memo of July 23<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d885-f5"/>—section <hi rendition="#italic">d.</hi></p>
                <pb facs="1018" n="824" xml:id="pg824"/>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">U. S. Property</hi>—Our two mimeographed memos: Germany
                    and satellites.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d885-f6"/></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">German External Assets—</hi>Proposed statement re vesting
                    of such assets,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d885-f7"/> and proposed directive to
                        General Clay re negotiations [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] of a vesting decree.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d885-f8"/></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Satellite Assets in Neutral Countries</hi>—Memo to
                        Molotov.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d885-f9"/></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Art Objects</hi>—Proposed directive to General Clay<anchor n="10" xml:id="d885-f10"
                    /> generally approving his proposal.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d885-f11"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
